      "side": 1,
      "message": "Passing capture type to the `fingerprint_get_info` command is not a good idea. Instead, the command could return array of capture type and their parameters.",
      "revId": "15171b9821500ac6699338d8b22ffb358ccbeb66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdb99a98_eb7ca10d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-27T00:56:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your suggestion requires a new `FpInfoCommand` version. I debated this with Tom, mainly adding `frame_size_raw`, `bpp_raw`, `bpp_simple`, `frame_size_simple`, etc. I believe the proposed solution is the easiest and most straightforward.\n\nThe `frame_size` and `bpp` returned by fpinfo, which we use in `ectool.cc` and `fpsensor_debug.cc` are no longer unified per a fingerprint sensor product with what Egis is proposing to do. So I believe the fpinfo should have the `capture_type` as input to return the correct sensor info.\n\nWe can keep the struct as it with the `bpp` and `frame_size` fields. We can just modify them for different capture types.",
      "parentUuid": "5831c797_04fcf157",
      "revId": "15171b9821500ac6699338d8b22ffb358ccbeb66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
